  "summary_en": "European Commission white paper proposing a dual approach: an 'ecosystem of excellence' to boost AI investment and uptake, and an 'ecosystem of trust' via a future risk-based regulatory framework for high-risk AI. It also examines gaps in EU product safety and liability law for AI and IoT, and opens public consultation until 19 May 2020.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Proposes a risk-based regulatory framework distinguishing high-risk from other AI applications by sector and use",
   "Mandatory requirements for high-risk AI: training data, record-keeping, transparency, robustness, human oversight",
   "Prior conformity assessment for high-risk AI; voluntary labelling for other applications",
   "Identifies gaps in EU safety and liability law for stand-alone software and AI",
   "Invests in research, skills, SMEs, and excellence centres; excludes military AI; consultation to 19 May 2020"
